// G10 schema addition. Purely additive: one new nullable/defaulted
// attribute on the already-existing HHG_InvestigationCase vertex type.
// No new vertex type, no new edge type -- HHG_INVOLVES and HHG_CITES
// already exist (declared in 02_edges.gsql, Phase D) and are reused
// as-is for affected_txn_ids / similar_prior_cases respectively; see
// docs/AGENT_WORKFLOW_SPEC.md Section 16 (G10) for the full design
// rationale (why edges, not JSON, for those two fields).
//
// first_suspicious_txn_id mirrors the existing flagged_txn_id UINT
// column exactly -- same type, same "pointer to one transaction"
// semantics -- required because the organizer's own Answer Format
// case.first_suspicious_txn_id field has no existing graph column to
// land in (confirmed during the G10 audit).
//
// Run once, against HHGOA_FraudInvestigation only. Never touches
// Transaction_Fraud or any other graph.

USE GRAPH HHGOA_FraudInvestigation

ALTER VERTEX HHG_InvestigationCase ADD ATTRIBUTE (first_suspicious_txn_id UINT DEFAULT 0);
